WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.067
Agent architecture.

2
00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:06.405
Strip away the hype, and every agent framework is one simple loop.

3
00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:07.200
Let's see it.

4
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.867
Here is the whole secret.

5
00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:13.233
An agent is a language model inside a while loop.

6
00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:19.033
LangGraph, CrewAI, AutoGen: all of them are this loop with opinions layered on top.

7
00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:22.067
Each iteration has three steps.

8
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:27.300
Perceive: read the current state, which is the message list, including tool results.

9
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.695
Plan: one model call decides to answer, or to request a tool.

10
00:00:31.695 --> 00:00:32.433
Never both.

11
00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:37.128
Act: your code runs the tool, and the result becomes the next perception.

12
00:00:37.128 --> 00:00:40.500
The loop exits when the model answers instead of acting.

13
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.467
Here is the part people miss.

14
00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:47.167
The model only emits decisions, as text or JSON.

15
00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:53.867
Your code owns everything that actually happens: execution, validation, retries, and termination.

16
00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:57.201
All of that is deterministic code you can test.

17
00:00:57.201 --> 00:01:00.300
Understand this, and no framework feels magical.

18
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.133
And here it is as real code.

19
00:01:03.433 --> 00:01:06.767
Inside a while loop, one model call plans the next move.

20
00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:11.100
If it asks for no tools, that is the final answer, and we break out.

21
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.567
Otherwise we run each tool, and append the result to the messages, ready for the next turn.

22
00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:19.833
Here is how to use this in practice.

23
00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:26.033
Before touching LangGraph, build the bare loop with one tool, a feed of near Earth asteroids from NASA.

24
00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:28.658
Ask: any hazardous asteroids this week?

25
00:01:28.658 --> 00:01:31.400
Watch it plan, act, perceive, and then answer.

26
00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:33.739
Keep that thirty line file forever.

27
00:01:33.739 --> 00:01:38.167
When a framework misbehaves, you debug it by mapping it back onto this loop.

28
00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:40.218
Let's recap.

29
00:01:40.218 --> 00:01:42.700
An agent is an LLM in a while loop.

30
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.300
Each turn it perceives, plans, and acts.

31
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.167
The model decides, and your code executes.

32
00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:52.329
And the loop exits on an answer, a step cap, or a stop rule.

33
00:01:52.329 --> 00:01:54.067
Next up: the ReAct pattern.
